From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: opencode-port <port@localhost>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 14:09:01 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] D211 core: compaction usage counts toward session statistics

Upstream: GET /api/experimental/session/stats adds compaction usage from stored session.usage.recorded event
payloads, but event persistence is opt-in (events.persist, off in every shipped host), so compaction usage never
reaches the totals: they disagree with the sessions' own cost and tokens. The upstream tests only passed because
they turn persistence on.
Fixed: stats read compaction usage from the compaction messages, which always record the total of their model calls
(cost and tokens), within the same time windows, project filter and fork rule as steps. Compactions are not steps.
Scenarios: session-api-transfer.test.ts "statistics after compacting imported history"
Upstream tests: packages/core/test/session-stats.test.ts updated (compaction usage now comes from compaction
messages instead of persisted events)

